        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: علت",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "علت ('ellat) — \"a cause, a reason\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "علت بیماری او هنوز معلوم نیست. 'ellat-e bimâri-ye u hanuz ma'lum nist. The cause of his illness is still not known."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural 'elal, an Arabic broken plural. Be 'ellat-e — because of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "علت ('ellat) comes from Arabic 'illa (EtymDB), a word for both a cause and an illness; in Persian it means the cause or reason for something."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
