          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عامل ('âmel) — \"a factor; an agent\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پول تنها عامل خوشبختی نیست. pul tanhâ 'âmel-e khoshbakhti nist. Money is not the only factor in happiness."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural 'avâmel, an Arabic broken plural. Also the person who does a deed."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عامل ('âmel) comes from Arabic 'āmil \"worker, doer\" (EtymDB): a factor is whatever does the work behind an effect."
            }
          ]
        },
